>Does Ultrix support NFS?

	Yes.

>Does Ultrix support both TCP/IP and DECNET protocols?

	Yes.

>Does rcp and rsh work from Ultrix to VMS?

	There is a tool called 'dcp' that lets you do the moral equivalent
of 'rcp' over DECnet. 'rcp' doesn't work over DECnet, nor do 'rsh'/'rlogin'

>How can I initate a file transfere from VMS to Ultrix?

	Depends on the protocol stacks you're running, but as long as you
are running one in common between the two, you can copy files. If you
have DECnet on both, you can use 'COPY' on the VMS machine and 'dcp'
on the ULTRIX machine. If you have TCP/IP on both you can use FTP to
transfer files, or NFS or (depending on the TCP implementation on VMS)
possibly 'rcp'

mjr.


