This is from the README-file together with the patches we have received
for 4.2A:


> /usr/ucb/ex			(CLD ipo04592)
> /usr/lib/ex3.7perserve
> /usr/lib/ex3.7recover
> ---------------------
> 
> vi core dumps when attempting to vi a large file from an nfs mounted file
> system from a CRAY.
>  
> The problem is vi doesn't check if the line buffer size is over the 8k limit.
> (the maximum size that ULTRIX vi can handle is 8k) Normally, this line buffer
> size (bsize) is set to optional blocksize for file system io ops (st_blksize)
> which in the case is 32k on the CRAY system.
> 
> Installation
> 
>         Replace the new ex:
>         # cd /usr/ucb
>         # mv ex ex.old
>         Now copy the new ex here
> 
>         To get edit, e and view create hard links:
>         # ln ex edit
>         # ln ex e
>         # ln ex vi
>         # ln ex view
> 
>         Replace the ex3.7perserve and ex3.7recover files:
>         # cd /usr/lib
>         # mv ex3.7preserve ex3.7preserve.old
>         # mv ex3.7recover ex3.7recover.old
>         Now copy in the new ex3.7preserve and ex3.7recovers here

You should be able to get this patch from your local supportperson.

