>Hi!  Does anyone know if the Prestoserve accelerator that ships with a number
>of DECsystems provide any help to Pathworks disk writes or only to NFS writes?

	It improves all synchronous writes. Since all file system meta data
(inodes) get written synchronously, you'll see an improvement in general
file system use. Stuff like removing large directories is *very* much
faster - so much so that if you accidentally type 'rm -rf' you've got a
slim chance of catching it with ^C. (I, uhhh, am NEVER so sloppy as to
actually type something like that by, uuuuh, accident - it's just that
at DEC we're so fast with our keyboards we do it as a way of showing
how much faster our reflexes are than a VAX9000... yeah, that's it!)

	I think you'll tend to see a slight speedup - 15% is a figure
that is a reasonable guesstimate for general common-or-garden activity.
Databases that write thier transaction logs synchronously will run
much faster. If you have an application that does many synchronous
writes with a high locality of reference, it'll really scream.

mjr.
