grabbing these characters.  For instance, I telnet from the DECstation to another
system.  I tell that system I have a vt100, emacs comes up in the DECterm window
and the crtl-s and ctrl-q doesn't work.  I don't remember where in the DECterm
menus that was the option to change the ctrl-s, ctrl-q behavior but once I found
it, those ctrl keys were passed on to emacs.  Maybe this is the situation you are
in?  Of course, X Windows emacs is unaffected.


