Greg,
 
There are at least two different ways to solve your problem.
 
In both cases, I would recommend creating a BACKUP saveset on the 
source VMS system as a first step. It is always easier to build a 
container file containing a large number of files than it is to 
move a blizzard of files either manually (or automatically) in a 
situation such as the one you describe.
 
First Alternative: 
 
Use FTP and COPY to move the resulting BACKUP saveset from the 
source machine to the destination machine as a binary file with a 
fixed record length. If necessary, use REBLOCK (which I posted 
the the net a couple of weeks ago) to temporarily reset the 
file's record size to 512 bytes. Then use BACKUP on the 
destination machine to "unpack" the files.
 
Second Alternative:
 
Convert the saveset to a HEX file (which only contains printable 
ASCII) and transfer it as an ASCII file over the network. When 
the file reaches the destination machine, convert it back to 
binary and unpack the saveset.
 
I generally use technique #1 to move files. I have had excellent 
success with using this method while retreiving savesets 
throughout the Internet (where the primary file transfer system 
is FTP).
 
I hope that the above is helpful.
 
- Bob
