In answering a question about how to clear the new mail count, in article 
<1992Jun23.201704.23712@engage.pko.dec.com>, calandra@fixes.enet.dec.com ()
writes...
> 
> 
>$ MAIL
>MAIL> read/new
>MAIL> exit
>$ Mail
> 

That isn't quite correct, and will work only when there isn't actually any new
mail.  It is necessary to read all the actual new mail and then execute
READ/NEW one more time, thus:

$ MAIL
MAIL> read/new
...
MAIL> read/new
No more messages        ! <-- This message will eventually appear, then:
MAIL> read/new
No new messages         ! <-- The count has now been zeroed
MAIL> EXIT
$


