Folks,

  Just as a general piece of information I wanted to provide pointers to some
information around TURBOchannel and TURBOchannel based products. 


TURBOchannel: 

	Is a 32bit synchronous I/O channel that is currently used on products
	in the VAX, MIPS and ALPHA architectures. It is used in both the
	workstation and server based systems. Software support for VMS, Ultrix
	and OSF/1 will be provided for the applicable systems under thos three
	architectures. For specific product information contact your local DEC
	sales person.

	Use of the TURBOchannel does not require any license or fees. It is
	free to both option and system vendors alike. The documentation that
