To All,

There has been an incredible amount of concern about recent articles which
indicated that Digital would not offer OSF/1 on the current and future 
DECstation workstations.  

I apologize for the delay in responding to your individual requests, but the
decision was just made and confirmed yesterday by the Executive Committee
within Digital.  I feel the decision was the correct one.  In summary:

* Digital WILL support OSF/1 on DECstations
* Digital will also support ULTRIX on current and future MIPS-based workstations

In effect, Digital will provide compatible environments on current and
future workstations.  Please call (or e-mail) if you have questions.

I've attached the original memo I received today as well as some answers
to questions posed as a result of this announcement.

regards ... jay

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
From: Charlie Christ, Vice-president SME/Departmental Systems and Software
To: All Field personnel
Subject: Digital's OSF Statement of Direction


Digital's direction for the OSF operating system on DECstations and DECsystems
is as follows:

1. Digital will implement the OSF/1 operating system on R2000, R3000, and 
R4000-based DECstations and DECsystems. This implementation
of OSF/1 will be compatible with the OSF/1 for Alpha-based systems.

2. Digital will support the ULTRIX operating system on R4000-based
DECstations and DECsystems. Today's ULTRIX applications will be binary-
compatible with R4000 systems running ULTRIX.

3. Digital will provide R4000-based CPU daughter card upgrades for the 
DECstation 5000 models 20, 25, 33, 120, 125, 133, and 240; the DECsystem
5000 models 25, 133, 240; and the DECsystem 5900.

Digital is committed to provide these products to our customers.


Commitment to OSF

Our customers have made their wishes known; they want OSF technology from
Digital, and they want it on multiple platforms. We will satisfy this
demand by providing the OSF/1 operating system for Digital's MIPS-based 
and Alpha-based systems. 
 
Our commitment to OSF gives our customers a complete array
of solutions at every point in the price range. This common software
environment enables customers to choose the time at which they can add
Alpha-based systems to satisfy their business requirements. 
This approach will make that coexistence and migration very easy 
and convenient.


******************************************************************************

* What is Digital's UNIX strategy?

Digital will provide the leading implementation of OSF/1, and continue our 
track record as the first vendor to bring OSF technologies to the market. 

Digital will continue our commitment to the MIPS processor family by providing 
R4000 CPU daughter cards, and a family of packaged R4000-based systems.

Digital is moving forward on the introduction of a complete range of 
Alpha-based systems that will run OSF/1.

Digital will provide a complete array of migration and coexistance options that
will enable customers to get the most out of their MIPS- and Alpha-based
systems in a common computing environment.

* Will ULTRIX applications migrate easily to these releases of OSF/1?

ULTRIX is binary compatible with OSF/1 on DECstations and DECsystems.
The application migration will be very easy.

* What about moving OSF/1 applications from MIPS-based systems to Alpha-based
systems?

Both hardware platforms will run the same version  of OSF/1, so the software
migration will be relatively simple.

* Will we implement ULTRIX on Alpha?

No.

* What about ULTRIX on VAX?

Our strategy has been to transition ULTRIX and System V UNIX on VAX to
OSF with ULTRIX and System V compatibility. This is still our strategy.

