The *only* thing that cannot be taken out of a current DS200 or a
DS240 is the memory. ALL turbochannel cards will go straight in,
so will all SCSI disks, display controllers, monitors. So to
upgrade to Alpha from DS200 will only require the purchase of
a new motherboard + memory.

If you want to put 256Mbytes of memory into Alpha, you *have*
to wait. The alpha box will hold 2 internal disks [of upto
2.8Gb], so to make room, they had to get rid of some memory
space. With the 32Mb memory boards, it will only take 128Mb
of memory right now. But, when alpha is shipped, 128Mb boards
will be available [using 16Mb drams] so that you can add upto
512Mb of memory in to the same box.

Of course, only the desktop has the 4 slots for memory. The
deskside and other models have much more already. The second
paragraph applies to desktop alpha models only.

