Ok, I did some mistyping on entering my article, what I really
want was the following NSAP:
39276F31000111000001890001AA00040008A000

The IDI for AFI 39 is 3 digits, but because there are two Octetts used,
it would be left bounded, and the filling is with 'F', according to
IS 8348 Ad 2.

When I try to use the DNA syntax, NCL continues to give me the MISSINGRIGTHBKT
error (what a wonderful error message!).
I've tried the following:
NCL>set routing manual network entity title {39:276:31000111000001890001:AA00040008A0:00 }

This should be correct according to DEC's Manuals, but MISSINGRIGTHBKT.

Guillaume Gerard from the French Telecom University gave me a good hint,
the following worked:

NCL>set routing manual network entity title {/39276F31000111000001890001AA00040008A000 }

Besides that, our network support center told me, that they indeed have
some ESIS routers running (not really routers, as they have only one interface,
but ESIS is enabled). The VAX didn't see them, as long as I had 
DNA Address Format = true, and no manual NET entity.

