Date: 16 Jun 92 17:51:03 -0700
Organization: Malaspina College
Lines: 32


I'm trying to figure out if it's possible to connect an RZ58 disk to
a VAX 4000-200 via an Emulex UC08-III. I don't have the RZ58 yet and
don't want to buy one if it won't work, so I can't just try it :-)

According to the Emulex manual the UC08-III supports SCSI, based on
ANSI X3T9.2/82-2 Revision 17B (16 Dec 85.) . DEC says the RZ58 is
a SCSI-2 device, which I gather from "Small Computer System Interface:
An Overview" [DEC P/N EK-SCSIS-OV-001] is based on ANSI X3T9.2/89-042.
From what I can gather from these documents the two devices are compatible,
but I'd feel a lot better if someone could acutally verify they work
together, or tell me if there are specific things I should check for
to determine if it's likely to work. I'd like to be able to boot the system
from this disk ( the UC08-III is an MSCP emulator and I've booted an RRD40
attached to it, so it appears reasonable to expect it to boot RZ58's ).

The reason I want to do this is because the $/MB for SCSI disks is about
1/2 to 1/3 the cost for DSSI disks and the SCSI disks could presumably
be used on a wider range of systems if we re-configure later (eg MV3100s).
We currently have RA disks on this system, but want to get rid of them
for various power/performance/maintenance cost/etc reasons. As far as I
know DEC only has the KZQSA adapter and I don't think it's appropriate
to use it in this case ( the S&O catalogue says you can't use this device
to attach RZs to a VAX and in any case I've heard its performance is
pretty awful )

These would be used with VMS V5.5.

