Udo,
 
The answer is yes and no. Using base VMS and DECnet, it is not 
possible to do a remote mount outside of an LAVc environment 
(however, there is an NFS like product, known as Distributed File 
Services, with a remote mount type capability).
 
However, you can use a logical name to point to a different node 
on your network. When the file is opened, the record management 
software will automatically establish a network connection to the 
machine which the file resides on. While this is not technically 
a MOUNT, it is, for most purposes, almost equivalent. For 
example:
 
        $ ASSIGN "nodename""user password""::" NODEX
        $ SET DEFAULT NODEX
        $ MACRO X
 
will use the Macro-32 assembler to assemble file X.MAR located in 
the user's account on node -nodename-.
 
I hope that the above information is useful.
 
- Bob
