Despite VMS being the same, there _are_ differences.  Not least because
Alpha VMS is stuck in a 5.4 timewarp just now (I don't know, and
probably couldn't say if I did, precisely what the relationship will be
come customer ship). 

> So, I believe it is an order of magnitude easier to port from VAX/VMS
> to Alpha/VMS because the operating systems are the same.

The problem is that people tend to use VMS' facilities assuming
atomicity in all sorts of horrible ways.  Fine on a VAX, which offers 
all sorts of atomic operations, but a real pain on an Alpha, where you 
have to think _real_ hard about parallel access to variables in your 
code.  Go back and look at that architecture manual again, and think 
about it...

That, and the sloppy alignment that many people feel encouraged to use on 
VAXs, are going to be the cause of many a slip 'twixt cup and lip...
