We don't use our LPS40 quite that much, only about 30,000 pages per
month, but we still have lots of problems with it.

> Also would be interested in finding out if there are any
> other good printers that may be able to supplement our
> current environment.  DEC is our first choice because we
> have very easy purchasing, and on site maint.

We recently (in the last two weeks) bought two QMS PS1700 printers, with
Ethernet interfaces and DECnet .  They are rated at 17 pages per minute,
and 50,000 pages per month.  They come with a software like CPS which
creates queues for several different emulations, including LN03+ with
DECTEK-4014, HP PCL, HPGL, and CCIT Group IV fax, as weel as the native
postscript.  The thing I really like about these printers is that it
is the printer itself which emulates the other printers, unlike the CPS
software which uses the VAX to translate to PostScript.

The internal processor in the printer is an Intel 80960 RISC chip, so
the LN03+ emulation is faster than a true LN03+, and much faster than
our old LPS40.

In fact, these printers can automatically select the proper emulation by
looking at the first block of the printed data.  This 'ESP' also works
with the Serial, Parallel and Apple Talk inputs which come standard with
the printer, so I had a demo set up where I just plugged it in in place
of an LN03+, and we were able to use the same print queue to print our
standard reports (which are TEK 4014 graphics), and PostScript files.

The printer uses the standard HP Laserjet cartridge so supplies are
readily available, and the cost of the two printers was about what one
LPS20 turbo would cost.

Good luck in your choice.

Ari
