  The SCSI implementation on Alpha/OSF is going to be SCSI CAM. This should
  continue to make life easy for the SCSI option vendors (and end users) who
  are currently working with the SCSI CAM interface on Ultrix and OSF/1. It
  is my understanding that the OpenVMS folks are going to be using the same
  open SCSI interface that they have for the last two years (documentation on
  which can be found in   gatekeeper:pub/DEC/TriAdd   for your amusement).

> The TURBOchannel is the same EXACT TURBOchannel used in the DECstation
> 5000/2xx series.  We couldn't change this bus and kill the work that a large
> number of TRI/ADD third parties have done in getting their products
> onto the TURBOchannel, it wouldn't make sense.  Add to that, we're not 
> in the business or re-inventing lots of things like TURBOchannel FDDI, 
