Such conservative limits are encountered more often in DEC software. Two further
examples:

- the total lenght of the argument list for the ld command cannot exceed 10K 
  characters according to DEC. In reality, trouble shows up at some 19K, but
  anyway one has a totally unreasonable limit for a number of object files to be
  linked. On Sun this limit is 1M characters. Fortunately, there is a work-around 
  by incremental linkage using -r option;

- there is a limit for the lentgh of a string assigned to a variable. When used
  e.g. within makefiles to collect a list of object files, make dies with
  segmentation fault without a warning whatsoever. A work-around may be very
  tedious here.

