>I don't know about VAX/Ultrix & Alpha/whatever, but I'd hope that location 0
>would be inaccessible, the VMS method is very useful for trapping programming
>mistakes with pointers.

The first virtual page on Alpha VMS is normally inaccessable, except in 
the case of a translated program in which the original VAX image had 
pages on what would be on Alpha the first page.  For example, many VAX 
images start at 0x200.  Therefore, on Alpha the translated image would 
use page 0, and so this trapping method won't work for translated images.

