What makes you say that?  VMS currently lets you get away with any sort of
data alignment you like, RISC processors tend to choke (especially RISC
processors without byte and word load/store instructions, which I believe
Alpha's is).  System calls also tend to accept 16 and 32 bit parameters,
which DEC can support for now but will need to change at some point to get
the most out of a 64 bit processor (which their competitors will force them
to do).  There are a lot of CISC versus RISC issues which DEC will have to
deal with in some way, and I am sure DEC will have to choose the RISC way
in some cases, ease-of-porting be damned.

I expect the migration from Solaris 1 to Solaris 2 to be far less painful.
