I recently poked through ULTRIX telnetd sources; their binary mode is
flawed and does not properly deal with raw carriage returns.  If your
binary sender includes something like "foobar\rquux", the receiver will
see "foobar\r\0quux".

With source, the fix is obvious (test for binary mode in the code doing
that conversion on the outgoing side).  Alternatively you can take a
more recent telnetd (say, BSD net 2) and use that.

[I have reported this bug to DEC]
