I get that error whenever I specify too many bytes in my NSAP for the AFI. I'm
not familiar with AFI 39, so I can't swear that this is the problem, but I'd
check it out closely. 18 bytes may be too big for that AFI. Also, I think you
may have one too many ":"s. I don't think you want one between the 00 and the
AA. This is normally all part of the local ID part of the DSP. I'm also not too
sure how the syntax of ":" is used in parsing. I know dashes are ignored.

