My problem was that the ftp program supplied with the above systems
seems to create big loads on the system, when a user leaves it in the
background and exits.

I got several replies from people which said they had the same
problem. as I didn't such a problem on our SUNs or SGIs I assume it is
a bug in the DEC ftp. 
What seems to happen is that when the ftp finishes and the user has
left it enters a tight loop, instead of shuting down. 
The solution: compile your own ftp. I took one from uunet.uu.net
in the directory /networking. It works fine and the problem
disappeared.

People also reported this to happen with WordPerfect being used over
modems, and the DECnet/Internet Gateway software that DEC supplies
with Ultrix, but I can't help on these (We don't use them).

