Hello named gurus,

recently we updated our VAXstation 3100 from Ultrix3.1 to Ultrix4.2.
The VAXstation is our primary nameserver and mail exchanger. We serve
some other locations as secondary nameserver. Both services ran
on Ultrix3.1.

We ran bindinstall and copied the old namedb to the new operating
system. Surprisingly we had to add the Official hostnames of
our feed hosts for the secondary databases to "/etc/hosts" (this was
unnecessary on Ultrix3.1). Otherwise named exits with an error
in syslog ("primary nameserver not in local db").

After this, named runs good using DEC's and SGI's - but using
SUN's nslookup on 4.1.1 and 4.1.2, our primary server is not accepted
and the secondary server (a Sun) is used.

  wega$ nslookup
  *** Can't find server name for address 134.60.1.1: Non-authoritative answer
  Default Server:  theophys.physik.uni-ulm.de
  Address:  134.60.10.1
  > 
  
We can switch to our primary nameserver by nand using nslookup's "server"
command. 

How can we solve this problem?

Thanks in advance

R. Huober
