From: Charlie Christ, Vice-president SME/Departmental Systems and Software
To: All Field personnel
Subject: Digital's OSF Statement of Direction


Digital's direction for the OSF operating system on DECstations and DECsystems
is as follows:

1. Digital will implement the OSF/1 operating system on R2000, R3000, and 
R4000-based DECstations and DECsystems. This implementation
of OSF/1 will be compatible with the OSF/1 for Alpha-based systems.

2. Digital will support the ULTRIX operating system on R4000-based
DECstations and DECsystems. Today's ULTRIX applications will be binary-
compatible with R4000 systems running ULTRIX.

3. Digital will provide R4000-based CPU daughter card upgrades for the 
DECstation 5000 models 20, 25, 33, 120, 125, 133, and 240; the DECsystem
5000 models 25, 133, 240; and the DECsystem 5900.

Digital is committed to provide these products to our customers.


Commitment to OSF

Our customers have made their wishes known; they want OSF technology from
Digital, and they want it on multiple platforms. We will satisfy this
demand by providing the OSF/1 operating system for Digital's MIPS-based 
and Alpha-based systems. 
 
Our commitment to OSF gives our customers a complete array
of solutions at every point in the price range. This common software
environment enables customers to choose the time at which they can add
Alpha-based systems to satisfy their business requirements. 
This approach will make that coexistence and migration very easy 
and convenient.


