Dave,

  I'm going to stick to the second question you pose. Recommendations that
I would make around installing to your Micropolis drive are:

	* Call the Micropolis Hotline and ask them if there is a DEC version
	  of firmware for this disk drive (Micropolis usually does have one,
	  the same as they do for IBM, HP and Sun).

	* Take a look at   gatekeeper:pub/DEC/ultrix-disktabs  and see if an
	  entry already exists for the drive you want to play with (or you
	  can probably use those entries to figure one out).

	* Think carefully about what layered products you want to install as
	  150MB is not a lot of space (comparative to what I use...but I am
	  unashamedly spoiled and usually install more subsets than I decline)
	  so you want to tailor this very carefully (in fact, I'm not sure if
	  you can really make a very fun system out of this. But I'm not sure
	  what your target is).

  Ultrix is not inhibited from being installed on foreign drives. We try to
make sure that it's as simple as we can. I hope this helps.

				Thanx,
				  AJ

p.s. One more item on v4.0, you won't find support there for disk drives over
     1.0GB in size. At that point in time we were still using a 6b addressing
     scheme which only supported a 1.0GB formatted disk.


