have to try for yourself and to your own satisfaction.

I'm pretty sure the VAX 4000/300 is in a box that has a Q-bus
on it.  I think the KDA50 most suitable for that box is the
-SE version, but my usually handy on-line price list isn't
available at the moment.  There's one version of it that is
factory installed when ordering new systems that support it
and another for field installed.

Where you would put the RA81 is an interesting question, since
there certainly not room in the usual boxes.  It's also not the
sort of disk I'd want in the office next to me.  If you're putting
the VAX 4000/300 in a computer room, then this isn't likely to be
