From the man page (V3.1 but I don't think it changed in this regard):

     f77 does not process the following options, but passes them to the cc(1)
     compiler:
[...]
     -S           Creates assembler .s file. (No link occurs.)

I.e. it is silently ignored since it was assumed you wanted -S passed on for 
any .c files.  The DEC Fortran compiler's technology does not generate 
assemblable files.  You can see the machine code using -V -show code and 
display the resulting .l (ell) file.

