	Well, as you're using emacs, you may want to use Alt as the Meta
Key, so you don't need escape as much, and just use F11 as escape when
nessesary. The problem you do have is that emacs assumes that whatever is
defined as mod1 is the Meta key, but mod1 are th compose keys and mod2
are the Alt keys. To get around this you do something like this:

	xmodmap -e "clear mod1" \
		-e "clear mod2" \
		-e "keycode 172 = Meta_L Alt_L" \
		-e "keycode 178 = Meta_R Alt_R" \
		-e "keycode 173 = Multi_key" \
		-e "keycode 177 = Multi_key" \
		-e "add mod1 = Meta_L Meta_R" \
		-e "add mod2 = Multi_key Multi_key"

to swap the mods around. Note the keycode lines are not really nessesary,
I put them in more for testing than anything else (before I found out about
emacs's assumption about Meta keys being mod1, as they were originally
bound as "Alt_L Meta_L". Doesnt seem to make any difference either way.)

[ ... Digression on pet peeve follows ... ]
