Note that "set def" can work in non-obvious ways; one that I find useful
is accessing one of my proxy accounts over DECnet.  Say I'm on SYS4:: and
I want to check a few files in one of my accounts on another system:

	SYS4> set def sys1::u2:[thad]
	SYS4> show def
	  SYS1::U2:[THAD]
	SYS4> dir
	SYS4> type foo.c
	SYS4> set def dev:

(where "dev:" essentially "returns" me back to where I was previously).

